process-owned-arrays.m's worker spawned on the machine's GPU. Each pass's
1.6 MB vault is freed by the pass that takes it, and each array that grow
outgrows by the resize, so the most that the worker holds at once is
grow's last array and the one it grows from, rounded up to the cache of
large blocks' sizes, with a few small blocks: 10 MB. Without the passes'
frees it held 47 MB, the sixteen vaults; without the resizes', 14 MB.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-owned-arrays.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-owned-arrays.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PROCESS_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK:27200000
CHECK-NEXT:79999800000
CHECK-NEXT:Merkurius runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
CHECK-NEXT:Merkurius runtime: a GPU process held at most {{104[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} bytes of blocks at once
